# Secrets
.env

# Spec Markdown
job-scout-spec.md

# Data and output — track feedback only. The database is never committed:
# it carries the full description of every ingested listing, and publishing
# ingested source content from a public repo is not ours to do.
data/*
!data/feedback.yaml
digests/

# The A2 regression corpus's posting text (#96). Same rule as the database above,
# and for the same reason with one addition: these are third-party copyrighted
# postings naming real contact persons, and this repo is public. The committed half
# is tests/fixtures/scored_postings.yaml — the manifest, which carries scores, bands
# and the rule each case exercises, and no posting text. Kept as a whole-directory
# rule with no `!` exception: a negation here is one careless pattern away from
# whitelisting the text back in, which is why the manifest sits outside the directory
# rather than inside it. Enforced by tests/test_repo_invariants.py.
#
# This holds regardless of how little text a fixture ends up carrying. Excerpting to the
# rule reduces the exposure; it does not make third-party text something a public repo
# should carry, and "it's only a few clauses now" is not a reason to revisit this line.
tests/fixtures/scored_postings/

# Local hand-scored label batches — the maintainer's own extractions from the private
# evaluation log, one JSON object per posting. They carry `justification` strings that
# quote posting clauses verbatim and `handle` fields that are the posting title, so they
# fall under the same rule as the fixture bodies above. First instance was the 28-row
# batch assessed on #133; a glob rather than one filename because the next batch should
# not depend on somebody remembering this line.
*.local.jsonl

# Per-issue agent briefs. They live in `docs/` for convenience but carry the same
# third-party posting text the rule above keeps out — `docs/issue_96_agent_brief.md`
# holds verbatim excerpts from five postings. Untracked today, and one `git add docs/`
# away from not being. A glob rather than one filename: the exposure recurs with every
# brief, and the next one should not depend on somebody remembering this line.
docs/*_agent_brief.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local memory
.claude/

# HuggingFace model cache
.cache/

# Codex
AGENTS.md
